Section D records the accuracy posture for the Section Seven Traffic signs dossier. Every knowledge fact is required to trace to its cited physical handbook page, with the cited page stating the fact. Confidence is high across the section because every rule comes from the single pinned handbook edition, and every number is spelled out in words so that the card backs read aloud exactly. The extracted text of these pages carries a font-encoding shift that garbles scattered words into offset letters and turns commas into line breaks, and the pages are picture-heavy with captions that the extractor interleaves; the dossier author decoded the shift deterministically, matched each caption to its sign by the surrounding text, and names every sign by shape, color or message so that no statement depends on a picture the learner cannot see. The sign images themselves are not reproduced. Handbook wording is paraphrased throughout; no official sentence, table, image or question is reproduced. No time-variable or location-variable fact appears beyond the pinned edition, so nothing required isolation as dynamic knowledge.
